// AUREUM AUTHORIZER-WINDOW / AureumGovernanceAuthorizer -- Act behavioural
// specification. PB2.12f / PB-D17 (Stage P-bis workstream A, formal-methods
// bundle; the S8-relabeled fourth surface).
//
// Dialect: Act v0.2.0 (argotorg/act), grounded against the shipped pass-tests;
// only operators witnessed there are used.
//
// Status: audit-handoff artifact; machine-checking firm-side per PB-D17(ii).
// Local verification cross-ref: test/formal/AuthorizerProofs.sol proves the
// P-W1..P-W4 cohort against the compiled bytecode -- hevm 0.58.0, bitwuzla
// 0.9.1, all PASS.
//
// This contract carries ZERO mutable storage: GOVERNANCE_CONTRACT,
// EMERGENCY_MULTISIG, EMERGENCY_WINDOW_END_BLOCK (block.number at construction
// plus EMERGENCY_WINDOW_BLOCKS = 2628000, one year OQ-5), and the two emergency
// action-ID hashes are all immutables (code, not storage), computed once in the
// H13-safe constructor with no external call. There is no state machine to
// model -- the sole behaviour canPerform is a pure view, stated in the residual
// footer below.

contract AureumGovernanceAuthorizer

constructor(address governanceContract_, address emergencyMultisig_, address vault_)

iff
  governanceContract_ != 0
  emergencyMultisig_ != 0
  vault_ != 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// canPerform(bytes32 actionId, address account, address where) : bool --
// RESIDUAL (environment read, firm-side per PB-D17(ii)).
//
// Not modelled as a transition returns: the emergency clause reads
// block.number, placed outside the witnessed single-contract fragment per the
// ema_sampler.act precedent. Note there is NO external call -- this is a pure
// view whose only non-witnessed element is the block-number environment read,
// so the firm's model may express it directly if its v0.2.0 grammar witnesses
// the block-number reference. The complete behavioural contract, with
// B := block.number and W := EMERGENCY_WINDOW_END_BLOCK:
//
//   governance : account == GOVERNANCE_CONTRACT ==> true, unconditional and
//                window-independent (no block, no action-ID constraint).
//   emergency  : account == EMERGENCY_MULTISIG, actionId in
//                { EMERGENCY_ACTION_PAUSE_VAULT,
//                  EMERGENCY_ACTION_ENABLE_RECOVERY_MODE }, and B < W ==> true.
//   time-bomb  : the strict inequality B < W makes the emergency role die at
//                EXACTLY B == W (the deploy block plus 2628000) and permanently
//                after -- every input is immutable, so no revival path exists.
//   default    : every other (account, actionId, block) triple ==> false.
//
// The two action-ID immutables follow the Balancer Authentication encoding:
// keccak256 of the vault-address disambiguator concatenated with the target
// selector (pauseVault, enableRecoveryMode).
//
// K7 MIGRATION NOTE: Vault.setAuthorizer(this) installs this authorizer on the
// byte-identical Balancer Vault. That call and the Vault-side canPerform
// dispatch are audited Balancer substrate (CLAUDE.md section-1 inheritance
// posture), outside the Aureum-artifact scope.
//
// Properties already proven locally against bytecode (hevm, bitwuzla):
//   P-W1 : governance authority is unconditional and window-independent.
//   P-W2 : both emergency actions live strictly inside the window; dead at the
//          boundary and forever after; scope limited to the two action IDs.
//   P-W3 : every non-principal account is denied every action at every block.
//   P-W4 : the two action-ID immutables match the Authentication encoding and
//          are distinct.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
